  "as_of": "2015-06-23",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would restore inflation indexation of excise-equivalent customs duties on imported fuels, validating higher collections authorised by tariff proposals from 10 November 2014.",
   "Future rates would rise with the consumer price index, generally twice each year in February and August, under changes to the customs tariff legislation.",
   "Aviation fuels would be excluded, while indexation of imported engine fuel ethanol would begin on the seventh day after Royal Assent under separate provisions."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The initial liquid fuel duty rate, excluding gaseous fuels, would be $0.386 per litre.",
   "Indexed customs fuel duty rates would be rounded to one decimal place of a cent.",
   "Transitional application rules would cover specified unpaid-duty stocks still under customs control."
  ],
  "affected": "Fuel importers and businesses claiming fuel tax credits for imported fuels are affected.",
