   "date": "2015-06-23",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "Labor supported the fuel excise indexation bills after securing a deal to direct the first two years of revenue ($1.1 billion) into the Roads to Recovery program, arguing this would boost jobs and local economies, particularly in regional and outer suburban areas. The speaker also criticised the government for cutting infrastructure investment and freezing financial assistance grants to councils, while committing Labor to future public transport investment."
